TEXT 0 232 Left 2 ;BROKEN: two ideal voltage sources with different values are wired
TEXT 0 264 Left 2 ;in parallel across the same node pair, so they disagree about what
TEXT 0 296 Left 2 ;V(Vout) is. There is no solution: the matrix is over-defined.
TEXT 0 328 Left 2 ;Fix: delete one source, or put a small series resistance in one
TEXT 0 360 Left 2 ;branch so the two can be reconciled by a current.
TEXT 0 392 Left 2 ;This is the fixture for a genuine SIMULATION failure, as opposed
TEXT 0 424 Left 2 ;to a static-check finding. Verified against LTspice 26.0.2:
TEXT 0 456 Left 2 ;exit code 1 and the log reads "Voltage source V2 and voltage
TEXT 0 488 Left 2 ;source V1 are paralleled making an over-defined circuit matrix."
TEXT 0 520 Left 2 ;Expected log finding: over_defined_matrix.
TEXT 0 552 Left 2 ;Note it still writes a .raw file despite failing, which is why
TEXT 0 584 Left 2 ;run_simulation must never infer success from the .raw existing.
